[Music]  i was delighted to serve as co-chair of  the president's committee on diversity  inclusion and belonging the work is very  important  for our society and for our university  but it's not easy  i was tremendously impressed by the  expertise generosity  and thoughtful contribution of each  member of the committee  each one of them brought a different  kind of expertise to the table  their knowledge and experience their  commitment to deep discussions  and their collective wisdoms allowed us  to continue our work during a very  challenging spring and summer  and to produce a report for president  salovey that i think we can all be proud  of  the report builds on previous university  initiatives  and proposes a forward-looking framework  i am confident  that the group's recommendations will  serve here well for many years to come  i'm ann curth the dean of the yale  school of nursing  it's a good moment to have this report  coming out the coven 19 crisis  has really demonstrated the racial  disparities in health care  that black indigenous people of color  and other populations have suffered from  in our country for many years  this is a timely moment it's a pivotal  one  the nation is calling for justice and  yale can respond  higher education needs to be a part of  this movement  at the school of nursing we are making  diversity equity inclusion belonging  and anti-racism work a priority because  we must reflect the communities we serve  in the way that we educate practice  and conduct research much learning has  to happen and i'm learning also  white people must listen with intention  to our bipod colleagues friends  students and loved ones we've spent 400  years centering white voices  now we must center in the voices stories  and narratives of our bipark  members and support  their needs to thrive  nothing less would be right  as an institution and as a larger  community  yale as always can lead by example and  take bold action  this report is a step in that direction  my name is darren lattimore i am deputy  dean  of diversity equity inclusion at the  school of medicine  i first want to say it was an honor to  be on the president's committee  each of us looks at these issues through  our own lenses  however it was immediately clear  that all of us felt a strong commitment  to creating a just environment  at yale university i also want to thank  our community  many of us interviewed students staff  and faculty in order to  get the information that we needed to  create the most robust plan  possible  i'm very grateful that i was on the  committee because at the same time  i was actually developing a strategic  plan  for the school of medicine it was really  helpful  to be able to see what the university is  doing in the dei  space as i created my plan because i  want to make sure that the strategies  that i use at the medical school  are in line with the strategies that the  university as a whole are using  and the outcomes that i'm measuring are  the same ones that the university as a  whole  are measuring i like to say  when we're all going in the same  direction working together  there's a much better chance that we'll  get the outcome that we want  hello my name is weylie chang i am the  executive director of the yale alumni  association  the mission of the yale alumni  association states  our character strength and values come  from our diversity and our commitment to  a culture of inclusion and equity  our mission is to enhance and renew the  lifelong yale experience  for all alumni whoever they are  and wherever they may be so who are  our alumni our alumni community is a  diverse group that spans  generations identities yale affiliations  and interests so a core value of the  yale alumni association  is inclusion what does inclusion mean  it means that we strive for full  engagement and a sense of belonging  among our alumni  all of our alumni have had the privilege  of experiences and  opportunities at and because  of yale these experiences and  opportunities  influence our choices and decisions and  in turn  these choices and decisions can  positively impact our communities  especially if there is an understanding  of diversity equity  inclusion and belonging  at this moment in time we have an  opportunity  and an obligation to advance these  important principles  they are priorities for the yale alumni  association  and for the university  i remember so clearly those meetings  after we received our charge from  president salovey  to shape the next phase of the  university's work on diversity equity  and inclusion  as well as belonging what a great  committee and we had some really  amazing conversations so many members of  the committee  have expertise in these areas or have  been citizens of the university for a  very long time  so they understand our culture we talked  often about how this  work is more of a marathon and not a  spread  we reviewed the work that has been done  by generations of students and faculty  staff and alumni  we talk to a lot of people on campus and  we compiled a pretty amazing list  of every project that's currently  underway or being planned  in the schools and in the administrative  units  i began to think of this whole project  differently  the committee's recommendations and the  president's priorities  not so much as a marathon but as a part  of a relay race  individuals complete marathons right  but teams actually compete in relay  races  and each person leg has an  individual contribution that's unique to  that person  so the committee's work is really about  passing the baton  the baton if you will toward a more  inclusive  a more diverse a more excellent yale  a yale where every member feels a sense  of belonging  and that baton has a common vision  a guiding principle and goals to align  the work  that's being done work that spans  schools and generations  identities and views that baton  also includes actions for the first five  years of this next phase  and all of this by the way can be found  online  yes we're moving into the next phase  of this race and we have the ability to  create  real change and together that is what we  will do  we all belong here we all belong to yale  so let's make sure that we show up for  ourselves and for each other  let's make sure that this part of the  journey counts

